                    <td class="num">{min30:.1f}%</td>
                    <td class="num">{min90:.1f}%</td>
                </tr>
"""

html += """            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="callout warning">
        <strong>Regulatory Footprint:</strong> Barcelona's 40.1% of listings requiring ≥30 nights is the clearest regulatory signature in the data, consistent with Catalonia's minimum-stay rules. Sydney's 16.1% requiring ≥90 nights suggests hosts are positioning listings for medium-term corporate or relocation stays, possibly to circumvent the 180-day annual cap. Paris's 11.5% requiring ≥90 nights may reflect "bail mobilité" (mobility lease) listings, which are explicitly noted in the dataset.
    </div>
</div>

